## Common Issues and Troubleshooting


If your setup isn't working (but your server is running), there are a few places to check first:


- **Is ngrok running? Is the URL properly set** in the *Voice Configuration* -> *A call comes in* section?
- **Do you hear dead air and no agent?** Your tunnel may rewrite the` Host` header. Set` PUBLIC_HOST` in your` .env` , and restart the server.
- **Was there an error with Twilio, possibly in your TwiML?** You can debug Twilio errors in a few ways –[there's more info in this article](https://www.twilio.com/docs/usage/troubleshooting/debugging-your-application) .
- **Is your Rime API key working?** Install the[Rime CLI](https://docs.rime.ai/docs/quickstart-cli) , run` rime login` , then` rime hello` .
- **Does Prism report an error?** Your console logs each Prism error with its code. Rime's[errors and limits docs](https://docs.rime.ai/docs/prism/errors#error-codes) explain the codes.
- **Does the assistant reply too early, or does it cut you off?** Prism might take a long pause as the end of a turn – tune that with the[turnDetection](https://docs.rime.ai/docs/prism/sessions#configure-a-session) option when you connect.
- **Did the call end after a quiet stretch?** Prism closes a conversation[after five minutes](https://docs.rime.ai/docs/prism/sessions#end-a-session) with no speech and no reply. Streaming silence doesn't keep it open.
- **Does your assistant remember nothing on the second call?** Check that memoryExtractionEnabled is on in your Conversation Configuration, it's off by default.


